// Windows: new local user account created
// MITRE ATT&CK: Persistence - T1136.001 Create Account: Local Account
// Attackers create accounts so they can get back in later. On a server where
// accounts rarely change, every new account deserves a look.
// Triage: who created it (CreatedBy), was it a planned change?
//
// Late-arriving data: agents can deliver events 10+ minutes late (e.g. right
// after a VM boots). The rule looks back 1 hour but only keeps rows that
// ARRIVED since the last 5-minute run, so each event alerts exactly once.
SecurityEvent
| where ingestion_time() > ago(5m)
| where EventID == 4720
| project TimeGenerated, Computer,
          CreatedAccount = TargetAccount,
          CreatedBy      = SubjectAccount
